    "intro": "Hi, I'm Laura, Mom, over-thinker, and the person who keeps forty tabs open on purpose. I have two kids, two dogs, everyone needs something. Usually while I’m in the bathroom. This is where I keep the songs, stories, lists and photos that would otherwise live in my head rent-free.",
    "bio": "I started MediocreMom because “doing my best” sounded like too much pressure, and “doing fine” seemed vague enough to get away with.\n\nI write, take photos, design things, and listen to music at a volume that suggests I’m trying to resolve some pretty deep-rooted issues. Give me power tools and I’ll build something. Give me five minutes online and I’ll develop a useless website.\n\nMy background includes interior design, tech, and customer support, so I can troubleshoot your problem, redesign the room you’re having it in, and quietly resent being asked.\n\nThis site is an outlet for thoughts that wander beyond the facts, lists that make life feel more manageable, photos, playlists sorted by mood rather than good sense, and the random bullshit taking up space in my head. It’s also home to a few creative ventures I’m building with a little grace and a lot of nerve.\n\nSome of it might be useful. Let’s not make that a requirement.\n\nMake yourself at home. The standards are already low.",
